  "comments": "The standard weight of these coins was 125 grains.<br /><br />\r\n1979D rims<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/639c7abf6bbf8.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/639c7abf6bbf8.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a><br />\r\n1979P types<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/639c7ad4b4e69.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/639c7ad4b4e69.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a><br />\r\n1979S types<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/639c7ae5dba80.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/639c7ae5dba80.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a><br />\r\n1981S types<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/639c7afc42dc2.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/639c7afc42dc2.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a><br /><br /><br />\r\nA very good site to see the differences between:<br />\r\n1979P far date/near the date<br />\r\n1979S type I/type II<br />\r\n1981S type I/type II<br /><br />\r\n<a href=\"http://www.smalldollars.com/dollar/page29.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://www.smalldollars.com/dollar/page29.html</a><br /><br />\r\nDue to the coin&#039;s similar size to the Quarter, it was badly accepted and eventually withdrawn. No coins were made for circulation from 1981-1998. Production resumed again in 1999 due to the introduction of the Sacagawea Dollar. Starting in May 2012, these coins began circulating in Ecuador, which has adopted the US Dollar as it&#039;s currency.<br /><br />\r\nMost of these coins bearing an &quot;S&quot; mintmark are not proofs. The San Francisco Mint struck this coin for circulation as well as all proofs for this type.<br /><br />\r\nType II coins show a clearer mint mark than the Type I issues.",
